 "ambiguities": [
  {
   "id": "supgp-extra-keys",
   "text": "SupGP CSV/JSON carry RMS and DATA_SOURCE, which are not OMM keywords (CCSDS 7.9.2.2 allows only Table 4-x keywords in an OMM); CelesTrak's CSV/JSON are OMM-keyword-based formats, not OMM instances, so this is a format extension rather than a violation. Parsers must tolerate unknown keys."
  },
  {
   "id": "tle-epoch-resolution",
   "text": "The TLE epoch has 1e-8 day (864 microsecond) resolution. CelesTrak GP epochs convert exactly between the two representations; SupGP epochs do not (86 microsecond difference observed), so a TLE->OMM epoch comparison needs a tolerance of half the TLE resolution."
  },
  {
   "id": "supgp-redistribution",
   "text": "SupGP data derives from operator-provided data (some explicitly 'with permission' to CelesTrak). Under the corpus design no raw bytes are shipped; the snapshot values for one SupGP record are published as a dated reference and may be removed by the owner before publication."
  }
